<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugen Zintgraff</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugen Zintgraff was a German explorer and colonial agent in Kamerun. In 1889 he reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamenda">Bamenda</a> grassfields and formed an alliance with Fon Galega I of Bali-Nyonga, aiming to recruit labour and open trade routes for German colonial interests. In 1891 his expedition with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a> allies was defeated by the Mankon and their neighbours, but the alliance made Bali the main German partner in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eugen-zintgraff.jpg" alt="Eugen Zintgraff" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown engraver 1899, Original uploader was Goerdten at de.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eugen_Zintgraff2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
